 id=\"text_8\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(292.249605 116.0032) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(120.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(141.515625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pc71921f0c0\"><rect x=\"39.962844\" y=\"12.32704\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · NPV ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Cash flow falls to $1.1M a year. NPV = −$15M + $1.1M × 9.82 = <b>−$4.2M</b>.</p> <p>Break-even: gate fees can fall to about 86% of today's level before the project stops paying.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the project's value depends on gate fees, which are not contracted and face new competition.</p>"},{"q":"What would you need before saying yes?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Long-term waste contracts</b> (10+ years) for most of the gate-fee income, at fees above 86% of today's</li> <li>Use more of the co-op's own manure and crop waste, so less depends on outside food waste</li> <li>A fixed electricity price contract if available</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Build the digester only once most of its waste is under long-term contract. The base case NPV is about +$1.7M, but gate fees are 40% of income, uncontracted, and likely to fall as three new digesters open nearby; if they halve, the NPV becomes −$4.2M. The project breaks even if gate fees stay above about 86% of today's level. Sign 10-year waste contracts and use more of the co-op's own manure before committing. Next step: approach the three largest food processors.","great":["Computes NPV with the lender's rate","Identifies the riskiest income stream","Finds the break-even gate fee","Makes the decision conditional on contracts"],"id":85,"slug":"fenland-biogas"}